# Build output. `make` writes into dist/, but a bare `go build` drops the binary
# next to the package it was run from — which is how gfk-gui.exe keeps appearing
# beside the Makefile. Paths are anchored so they cannot swallow cmd/gfk/, which
# is a source directory with the same name as the binary it builds.
/dist/
/go implementation/dist/
/go implementation/gfk
/go implementation/gfk-gui
gfk-linux-*
gfk-windows-*
*.exe

# Real configs. The *.example.yaml templates are tracked on purpose; a working
# client.yaml / server.yaml is not. Those carry your server's IP and auth.key —
# the shared secret is the only true credential in this project, and anyone
# holding it can use your tunnel.
client.yaml
server.yaml
*.local.yaml

# Field-test output. Captures are the most sensitive thing the project produces:
# a pcap of a live session contains the real endpoint addresses on both ends.
*.pcap
*.pcapng
*.log

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
